      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The Cochrane Collaboration uses rigorous and widely accepted methods, together with peer-review, to produce systematic reviews of all data of acceptable scientific quality relating to specified aspects of healthcare. Review Groups exist for a number of areas of medicine and surgery, but at present not headache. It is argued that there should be a Cochrane Collaborative Review Group for Headache, and that the International Headache Society should foster its creation. Some principles are set out. The step from establishing the evidence-base to incorporating it in treatment guidelines should be taken circumspectly."},
